  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. I've successfully added voucher support. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**New error code in `src/errors.js`:**\n- `VOUCHER_EXISTS` - invoice already has a voucher applied\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js` with:**\n\n1. **Modified `invoiceTotals()`** to include voucher:\n   - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n   - Calculation: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n   - Voucher is a fixed amount deducted after VAT\n\n2. **New `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })`** function:\n   - Validates:\n     - Invoice is draft (NOT_DRAFT error)\n     - No existing voucher (VOUCHER_EXISTS error)\n     - Amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n   - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n   - Preserves all other invoice fields (customerId, issueDate, status, lines, terms, dueDate)\n   - Does not mutate input\n\n**Key design:**\n- One voucher per invoice maximum\n- Vouchers only on drafts (before issuing)\n- Fixed amount in cents (e.g., $50 off = 5000 cents)\n- Applied after VAT, so VAT is calculated on full amount before discount/voucher\n\n**Tests:** 11 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Voucher reducing total correctly\n- Single voucher per invoice enforcement\n- Draft-only restriction\n- Amount validation (positive, integer)\n- Metadata preservation and immutability\n- invoiceTotals calculation with vouchers\n\nAll 162 tests pass.",
